 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-virginia/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is South Carolina cheaper than Virginia?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On most lines, modestly. The state income tax is close. South Carolina's deduction is larger than Virginia's for a couple earning up to about $126,000. Property tax on a primary home runs less than half, and a typical house costs about $76,000 less on the statewide averages. Sales tax is the line that goes up."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Virginia or South Carolina tax military retirement?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Virginia lets you subtract up to $40,000 of military benefits on 2025 and later returns, with no age requirement. South Carolina exempts every dollar of military retirement pay at any age, with no cap. Below $40,000 of military pension the two match; above it, only South Carolina exempts it all."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens to the Virginia age deduction when I move?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It stays behind, and for many retirees it was already gone: Virginia's $12,000 age deduction shrinks a dollar for every dollar of adjusted federal AGI over $50,000 single or $75,000 married, and is gone entirely at $62,000 and $99,000. South Carolina's retirement and age-65 deductions have no income test."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will I still pay an annual car tax in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and you already know the routine. Every vehicle is taxed on its value each year and the county bill is paid before the plate renews. A $30,000 car is taxed about $362 a year in unincorporated Horry County plus a $50 road fee, and a car titled elsewhere pays a one-time $250 fee at first registration."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a house cost in Myrtle Beach compared with Virginia?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical home here costs about $342,000 against a Virginia statewide average of about $418,000, on the same July 2026 Zillow measure. The statewide number hides the split between Northern Virginia and everywhere else. See how much further every dollar goes here on our cost of living calculator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax Social Security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No, and neither does Virginia, so that part of the move is neutral. The differences are in how each state treats the rest of retirement income, and in the property tax."}}]}</script>
