d never a listing number together with anything that identifies you.</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.35rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .75rem">The property analyzer and address lookup</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem">When you use the investment analyzer at <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--brass)">/invest/long-term-rental/</a> or type in its address box, the property address you enter is sent to third-party services so the tool can look up and analyze that property. We do not send your name, email or phone number to any of them.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 1rem 1.15rem"><li><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Anthropic</strong> (United States) receives the property address and the property details you enter, and returns the written analysis. Anthropic does not use data submitted through its API to train its models.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Cloudflare</strong> (United States) runs the service that makes these requests and stores the resulting analysis for up to twelve months, so that the same address returns the same numbers to everyone who looks it up. What is stored is the property analysis, keyed to the address. It is not linked to you.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy)">The United States Census Bureau geocoder</strong> converts an address into map coordinates.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Photon</strong>, an address-suggestion service operated by Komoot in <strong style="color:var(--navy)">Germany</strong>, receives what you type in the address box in order to suggest matching addresses. This means that text leaves the United States.</li><li><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Horry County, South Carolina</strong> public GIS records are queried for nearby building permits.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;margin-bottom:1rem">If you would rather not have an address processed this way, do not enter 